# The processes (roadmap os-server.md P6): init, process 1, starts
# tests/posix/proc.c from /z (TEST_POSIX_PROC), which forks, execs, spawns
# and waits, takes a child's fault and a kill as their signals, uses the
# heap, and is refused a fork once the table is full. The idle program
# waits for a key meanwhile; the test ends when the wait is over.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_PROC
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 180
---
proc: my parent is init (1): 1
proc: the child: its parent is the forker: yes
proc: a fork (3): exited 3
child: argc 3: /z/child 4 two
child: my pid is the one asked for: yes
child: environ[0] TEST=proc
proc: a fork and an exec (3): exited 3
child: argc 1: /z/child
child: environ[0] (none)
proc: the spawned (1): exited 1
proc: posix_spawn (0): 0
proc: an exec of no file (-1, ENOENT 2): -1, 2
proc: after it (4): exited 4
rx286: proc[7] fault #UD at 0007:{z:proc.rx_ud2}
proc: a child's #UD (SIGILL 4): ended by signal 4
proc: kill (0): 0
proc: the killed (SIGTERM 15): ended by signal 15
proc: kill init (-1, EPERM 1): -1, 1
proc: kill no one (-1, ESRCH 3): -1, 3
proc: 3000 bytes of heap: yes; the break moved: yes
proc: a fork bomb: 8 children, then EAGAIN (11): 11
proc: all 8 reaped; then ECHILD (10): 10
proc: done
